    "https://jobs.frankfurt-school.de/en/jobs/328/project-manager-senior-project-manager-mfd-frankfurt-school-of-finance-management": {
      "title": "Project Manager / Senior Project Manager (m/f/d) – Finance & International Projects",
      "description": "Project Manager / Senior Project Manager (m/f/d) – Frankfurt School of Finance & Management Project Manager / Senior Project Manager (m/f/d) – Finance & International Projects Frankfurt limited Professionals ab sofort 54,000.00 to 80,000.00 EUR gross per year Share this job! Shape the future of finance and education at Frankfurt School of Finance & Management! As a leading business school with an international outlook, we empower ambitious professionals to drive progress and bold innovation in banking, finance, and management. Our vibrant, inclusive environment in the heart of Frankfurt is the ideal place for experienced project managers who want to make a meaningful impact and continue developing in a dynamic academic context. Your Tasks Acquisition of complex new projects: compiling documentation for international tenders (expressions of interest, technical and financial offers) Conceptual design and/or implementation of new complex international consulting concepts/programmes/financing instruments/technical assistance applying latest standards and frameworks in sustainable finance Relationship management with and identification of new strategic customers incl. fundraising activities with international donors and governmental bodies and experts Management of projects/programmes, including provision of key content input, coordination of and correspondence  important stakeholders, ensuring solid operation and monitoring; i.e. high standards of project management Financial modeling, i.e. to assess financial viability and calculate financial indicators as well as other indicators relevant to public and private sector funded projects Development of new training concepts and products as well as preparation of training material Your Profile University degree in the area of finance and/or economics A minimum of 10 years of progressive work experience in an international setting, dealing with climate/sustainable finance and natural resources management Extensive experience with management, implementation and appraisal of projects in developing countries and emerging markets Experience in dealing with governments, private sector, international financial institutions, development finance institutions Very good understanding of the various aspects of climate and development policies as well as international climate change developments as well as knowledge of financing renewable energy and energy efficiency projects Commercial banking experience (product development, processes, risk management etc.) would be an advantage Languages: fluency in English, proficiency in German, French and/or Spanish is desirable Intercultural awareness, international mobility and ability to work under time pressure We Offer 30 days of annual leave, along with extra days off for special occasions : Whether it’s the end of the year, your wedding, a move, or your birthday – we give you the gift of time. This includes full days off on Christmas Eve and New Year’s Eve, plus a half day on your birthday and on Shrove Tuesday. Company pension scheme : We’re thinking ahead: with strong additional retirement benefits to secure your future Corporate benefit programme : Enjoy exclusive discounts for employees across a wide range of partner companies: from electronics to leisure activities Flexitime and time off to balance overtime : A balance of structure and flexibility: Our flexitime model within core working hours lets you compensate for overtime with additional time off Employee events and a strong team culture : From summer parties and Christmas celebrations to inspiring skill-sharing sessions: we believe in celebrating success together remote work in a 3–2 model : Flexible work model: Three days on-site, two days remote – supporting a healthy work-life balance Learning & Development : Learning is at the heart of what we do: Benefit from a wide range of learning and development opportunities – from internal training to LinkedIn Learning for flexible, self-paced learning Excellent transportation links : Ideally located with excellent access to public transportation smart AI solutions for everyday office work : Our advanced AI solutions streamline your workflow: so you can work faster and focus on what truly counts Exercise and fitness offers : Diverse sports options to help you stay active and recharge after work Discounted public transport ticket (Deutschlandticket) : Sustainable and budget-friendly travel with the subsidised Deutschlandticket Ready to take the next step in your career? Apply online now and become part of our dedicated team. We look forward to getting to know you. If you have any questions about the position or the application process, please don't hesitate to contact us. Gabriela Rack Personalreferentin/ HR Manager P: +49 69 154008 – 996 Back Apply Privacy | Data Protection powered by d.vinci"
    },
